    "narrative": "For July 12, 2026, **Seiya Suzuki** leads the Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup with an elite 75.03 efficiency score, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Abbott\u2019s 4.89 xERA and a potent #2 spot in the order. **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Mickey Moniak** also provide high-end production today. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup against Baz, while **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime \"green light\" position; he faces a slow-delivery pitcher that boosts his sprint-based stolen base probability, further elevated by his placement in the #2 hole. These plays anchor a lineup designed to maximize our daily cap efficiency while aggressively targeting SB opportunities.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Austin Riley**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 46.08 score. While his pedigree is undeniable, a combination of a pitcher-friendly park and a challenging wind-in scenario against May forced him to the bench in favor of **Kyle Karros** and **Isaac Paredes**, who maintained more stable floor projections. We are monitoring **Brice Turang** closely; while his 47.02 score earned him the start at 2B, he faces an elite test against Skenes. The -19% SP skill penalty and a difficult catcher hold time suggest we may see reduced stolen base output from him today. Managers should note that while the weather remains clear, the matchup against Skenes for **Brice Turang** and the potential for a sluggish outing from **Edwin Arroyo** against Boyd represent the primary risks to our 5x5 categories today.",
